;; ClojureDocs Entity-Attribute Model — EDN Schema
;;
;; Source of truth for the data model. Replaces entity-attribute-model.csv.
;; Generated from REPL-verified findings in dev/sidecar_repl.clj
;; See docs/rfcs/entity-model-rfc.md for design rationale.
;;
;; Verification split:
;;   JVM-heap entities (library, namespace, var) and the edn-file entity
;;   (dialect-compat) are checked against the running system by
;;   test/clojuredocs/entity_model_test.clj on every run.
;;   MongoDB entities (example, example-history, note, see-also, user,
;;   legacy-var-redirect) are snapshot-derived from sidecar_repl.clj and are
;;   NOT yet test-guarded — their cardinalities/coverage will drift (issue #66).
;;
;; Completeness: a :status of :exists means that attribute was verified PRESENT,
;;   not that the entity's attribute list is complete. No systematic search for
;;   gaps was performed — entities or attributes that exist but are not listed
;;   here would not have been caught. This records what was verified, not a
;;   guarantee that nothing is missing.
;;
;; Status semantics:
;;   :exists   — REPL-verified, data is there
;;   :nil      — key exists but value is systematically nil
;;   :vestigial — key exists but carries no meaningful information
;;   :absent   — key is retained by code (e.g. listed in search/var-keys) but no
;;               record in the current dataset carries it
;;   :planned  — has a GitHub issue tracking it
;;   :gap      — described in vision doc, no code or data yet
;;
;; Coverage: nil when :required? is true, otherwise n/total

